# Trivy exceptions for the authored AWS/EKS Terraform path (see
# docs/security.md "Documented exception path"). Each entry is narrow, has a
# justification, and is reviewed with the infrastructure change.
#
# AWS-0039 - EKS secrets encryption (KMS) is not enabled in the module.
#   Accepted for the portfolio path; the module is author-only (never applied).
#   Before using real data, add a KMS key + encryption_config to modules/eks.
AWS-0039
#
# AWS-0040 / AWS-0041 - EKS API endpoint is public (and CIDR-restricted via
#   `public_access_cidrs`; prod's default placeholder is 203.0.113.0/24, dev is
#   0.0.0.0/0 for demo access). Public access is required so Argo CD/kubectl can
#   reach the cluster without a VPN/bastion. Tighten the CIDRs (or set
#   endpoint_public_access=false) before any real deployment.
AWS-0040
AWS-0041
#
# AWS-0104 - the EKS-managed cluster security group allows unrestricted egress.
#   Required for managed add-ons, image pulls and AWS APIs; restricting it
#   reliably breaks EKS-managed traffic.
AWS-0104
